      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is happening to me all the time lately. I login from the game, SDK, and website from computer and phone sometimes. I do occasionally use a VPN so I wonder if my phone's cell connection or the VPN are registering as foreign devices and logging me out everywhere else. If that's the case it would be nice if we could get like a whitelisted devices/IP page that don't get signed out, and allow us to log out unwanted devices remotely. I assume the current behavior was implemented as a security measure for users allowing creators to login to their account for uploads, so the third party does not stay logged in. However I sometimes get logged out of the website when I'm not even accessing VRC from any other device or mode so I don't know. \n\nHaving to sign in again in the SDK, website, or desktop mode is not a big deal. Having to sign in from VR is a huge pain in the ass especially when it happens so frequently.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
